The current environment creates virtual machines on nodes in15 and in16. 
The virtual machines are named in15vm01, in16vm01, in15vm02, etc.
For ease of testing, I want to be able to ssh to these machines from my
laptop. In order to access them, I need to use ProxyJump directives in
my ~/.ssh/config to jump to comely.newmexicoconsortium.org, and then to
in-master, and then finally to in15 and in16.

Additionally, I want passwordless ssh to simplify testing and to enable
tools like ansible. So, the first thing I have done is ssh-keygen on
my laptop and then do ssh-copy-id of that to in-master, in15, and in16.
Then I do the same from in-master to in15 and in16 and from in15 and in16
to both themselves and to each other. At this point, the authorized_keys
files on in15 and 1n16 contain four entries.

Then, the setup_VM_batch.sh script copies those authorized_key files into
the VM's.

In order for host-resolution to work, I had to use libvirt-nss in combination
with Linux Name Service Switch on in15 and in16:
> sudo dnf install libvirt-nss
Edit /etc/nsswitch.conf to change the 'hosts:' line to add libvirt libvirt_guest
Test with getent hosts [domain_name]

Finally, because we always run as root within the VMs and because we want a
minimal number of ~/.ssh/config stanzas, we do the followin in the ~/.ssh/config
files in laptop, in-master, in15, and in16:

Host in15vm*
    User root
    ProxyJump in15

Host in16vm*
    User root
    ProxyJump in16

